unpack writes a new working copy and never writes over one. --refresh renders one again.

```console
$ stetdoc unpack contract.docx -o work
wrote work: document.md
base 5737b772923cf8d3:0:5737b772923cf8d3
next: stetdoc view work

$ stetdoc unpack contract.docx -o work
? 2
error[invalid_payload]: work already exists and is not empty, and stetdoc unpack writes a new working copy.
next: It is a working copy already: keep using it, choose another folder with -o, or run stetdoc unpack DIR --refresh to render it again.

$ stetdoc unpack work
? 2
error[invalid_payload]: work is a folder, and stetdoc unpack reads a .docx.
next: Name the .docx, or add --refresh to render this working copy again, discarding edits that were not packed.

$ stetdoc unpack work --refresh
rendered again work: document.md
base 5737b772923cf8d3:0:5737b772923cf8d3
next: stetdoc view work

```
